course: dictionary
lesson: 13583
title: Formal words about weather
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words belong to formal writing, such as letters, notices and news reports. Inclement is one of them. You do not need to know it before you read, because the words around it give you clues.
explain: «In the event of inclement weather, sports day will move into the hall.» The sports day moves indoors, so inclement weather must be bad weather that stops games outside. Check it by swapping in bad: «In the event of bad weather, sports day will move into the hall» still makes sense, so your meaning is right.
explain: Inclement is mostly used about the weather. It means cold, wet, stormy or unpleasant. In an old, rare use it can mean harsh or without mercy, but you will rarely meet that meaning.
fact: «Inclement» is an adjective, a describing word, and it is formal.
fact: «Inclement» means cold, wet, stormy or unpleasant, and it is used about the weather.
fact: «In the event of inclement weather» means «if the weather is bad».
fact: Phrase to learn: «inclement weather».
fact: Old, rare meaning: «inclement» can mean harsh or without mercy.
exercise: «The match was cancelled because of inclement weather.» What does inclement weather mean here? | Warm and sunny weather | *Bad, wet or stormy weather | Weather for swimming | Strange weather with no wind
exercise: A notice says: «In the event of inclement weather, the picnic will be held in the hall.» Where will the picnic be if the weather is bad? | At the top of the hill | Nowhere, because the notice is wrong | On the beach, because it is sunny | *In the hall, because the weather is bad
exercise: Find the word that means cold, wet and stormy. | gentle | cheerful | *inclement | sunny
test: «The farmer hoped the inclement storms would pass soon.» What does inclement mean here? | Very small | *Stormy and unpleasant | Quiet and calm | Bright and cheerful
test: Which phrase would a school notice use to mean «if the weather is bad»? | in the event of a bright morning | in the event of a sudden party | *in the event of inclement weather
exam: Which sentence uses inclement correctly? | The inclement puppy wagged its tail. | *We stayed indoors because of the inclement storm. | We ate an inclement sandwich for lunch.
